A friend of mine made the following assertions about NetHack and
Moria. I wonder if those of you with greater experience than I could
comment. I promised him that I'd ask:
 
"Nethack was one of the first games I played, back in high school. I
had quite a bit of fun with it, even though I died left and right. My
favorite trick was using wands of digging to break into stores so I
could steal stuff.
I discovered Moria a year or so later, and I liked it even more due to
the Tolkeinesque backdrop. I also appreciated its gameplay, which was
more straightforward than Nethack and more like I'd originally
envisioned a dungeon crawl game as being.

I started playing vanilla Angband in college, and I used to play it
quite a bit. I thought all the enhancements from Moria (especially the
boss monsters and artifacts) were wonderful. But then, a year or two
ago, I realized two things which have killed my desire to play that
game:

1. No matter what race/class you play, all characters end up being
almost the same at the end due to all the stat-enhancing potions that
you can pick up in the medium levels of the dungeon. Everyone ends up
with maxed-out stats, and minor racial bonuses aside, there's not much
difference between them. For some reason, realizing that all my
characters were the same really bugged me.
 2-Even with maxed out stats, you'll never be able to get strong
enough to whomp on the tough (level 65+?) monsters. That's partly true
because of the level 50 experience cap (which I hate), and partly true
just because your maxed-out stats still aren't all that great, and
because so many of the high-level monsters summon so often. I'd like
the game a lot more if there were a point where I could become so
powerful that I could just blow through large groups of powerful
summoned monsters. Basically, I'd like to have something like the
different difficulty levels of Diablo, where on the lower difficulty
levels I know I will eventually get strong enough (with constantly
increasing stats/hitpoints & better and better armor/weapons) to beat
up anything giving me trouble. I don't like having to use pillar
strategies every time I see a high-level summoning creature, nor do I
like having to run from anything (if you can kill Morgoth, you should
never have to run). It gets old.

Maybe there are variants out there that would fix all this for me, but
I could never find any. Most variants I looked at had too much added
stuff that I didn't want, also. I just want basic Angband/NetHack with
fixes to the issues I mentioned above.  Feel free to let me know if
I'm wrong/missing something."

